2026-07-21      Bogdan Drozdowski <bogdro #at# users . sourceforge . net>

	* ExpiryManager 0.7.1
	  Fix Manage Types list not refreshing after editing lead time.
	  Mutating the existing ProductType instance in place before saving
	  corrupted DiffUtil's "old" comparison snapshot: that instance was
	  the same object the adapter's currently-displayed list held, so the
	  refreshed Room query result compared equal and the row was never
	  re-bound until leaving and re-entering the screen. Building a fresh
	  instance for the update avoids sharing state with the displayed list.

2026-07-21      Bogdan Drozdowski <bogdro #at# users . sourceforge . net>

	* ExpiryManager 0.7.0
	  Show a product's container in the main list. Reuses the existing
	  detail line (type · quantity · unit), appending the container when
	  one is set instead of adding a separate row.
	  Add containers: where a product is stored. New optional, non-editable
	  dropdown field on Add/Edit (Fridge, Freezer, Pantry, Medicine cabinet
	  by default), populated only from a new "Manage Containers" screen,
	  mirroring how product types already work. Container values are
	  free-standing (not derived from products), so they survive product
	  deletion, and the field is clearable like the open-date field.
	  Also fixes the equivalent problem for product types: default-seeding
	  data in RoomDatabase.Callback#onCreate() only runs for a truly new
	  database file. fallbackToDestructiveMigration()'s upgrade path drops
	  and recreates tables on an *existing* file without calling onCreate(),
	  so an in-place update would have left both new tables' defaults empty.
	  Moved seeding to onOpen() (idempotent via CONFLICT_IGNORE), which runs
	  on every open regardless of how the schema got there.

2026-07-21      Bogdan Drozdowski <bogdro #at# users . sourceforge . net>

	* ExpiryManager 0.6.1
	  Fix open-date field's clear icon never appearing TextInputLayout's
	  built-in "clear_text" end icon only shows itself once the EditText
	  has focus, but the open-date field is intentionally non-focusable
	  (tapping it opens a date picker instead of a keyboard), so the icon
	  could never appear and there was no way to clear the field short of
